     • store-to-store[i][j] = distance(store_i → store_j)    // unneeded if i==j
     Actually we only need a flat vector `towns[S]`.

i.  compress: `int town[S]; i: store_list[i]`
    And compute `dist[i][j]` for all i,j in {0,1,…,S}
------------------------------------------------------

    vector<long long> town = store;                 // way short

